\ `while` and `loop` are row-variable loop combinators: each body ends in a
\ recursive self-call whose effect reaches below the word's declared inputs into
\ the symbolic row. Modeling that reach-below shape lets the AOT compiler emit
\ their word bodies as native C (the predicate and body quotations still run
\ through the interpreter) instead of rejecting them with an abstract underflow.
\ Built under runtime-image AOT, so these results come from the compiled
\ combinator bodies and match the interpreter.
0 [ dup 3 < ] [ 1 + ] while .
"--" print-line
0 [ 1 + dup 3 < ] loop .
